From b7421a67e7eaf4897ba35210cb12ef76420ccba0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonas Heinle <jonasheinle@googlemail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 20:21:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [ukernel] Drop inline from the s8s4s32 1x8x16 i8mm tile

mmt4d_arm_64_tiles.inl declares this tile through IREE_UK_MMT4D_TILE_FUNC_DECL
as a plain external function, and the entry point takes its address from
another translation unit. The definition is marked ALWAYS_INLINE inline, unlike
every other concrete tile function in the file, so under MSVC inline semantics
(clang-cl, arm64) no out-of-line copy is emitted and the tools fail to link on
the symbol.

always_inline does nothing here anyway: the function is only used by address.

Assisted-by: Claude (Anthropic)
Signed-off-by: Jonas Heinle <jonasheinle@googlemail.com>
---
 .../src/iree/builtins/ukernel/arch/arm_64/mmt4d_arm_64_i8mm.c  | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/runtime/src/iree/builtins/ukernel/arch/arm_64/mmt4d_arm_64_i8mm.c b/runtime/src/iree/builtins/ukernel/arch/arm_64/mmt4d_arm_64_i8mm.c
index 8582e07..7c2c5b7 100644
--- a/runtime/src/iree/builtins/ukernel/arch/arm_64/mmt4d_arm_64_i8mm.c
+++ b/runtime/src/iree/builtins/ukernel/arch/arm_64/mmt4d_arm_64_i8mm.c
@@ -115,8 +115,7 @@ IREE_UK_MMT4D_TILE_FUNC_IMPL_FOR_M0(
 // This int4 conversion trick is borrowed from the `qd8-f32-qc4w-gemm*`
 // kernels in https://github.com/google/XNNPACK.
 
-IREE_UK_ATTRIBUTE_ALWAYS_INLINE inline void
-iree_uk_mmt4d_tile_s8s4s32_1x8x16_arm_64_i8mm(
+void iree_uk_mmt4d_tile_s8s4s32_1x8x16_arm_64_i8mm(
     void* IREE_UK_RESTRICT out_tile, const void* IREE_UK_RESTRICT lhs_panel,
     const void* IREE_UK_RESTRICT rhs_panel,
     const iree_uk_mmt4d_params_t* params) {
